-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gunfright
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Gunfright (1985)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         0cd9e86a2c6c7afa22025f8d593af093

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The sheriff, townsfolk, horses and street bandits each painted
              in their own colours, the bandits dressed apart from the
              townsfolk; the buildings and street scenery painted; each of the
              twenty duel opponents in their own colours. Drawn on the Next's
              Layer 2 with no outlines added; the wanted poster, score and the
              rest of the screen keep the original's look. Source: Patch and
              colours: Jon Attree, painted over the original game's own
              figures.

  Pace        original (-1.08% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe A3C6
              (the player's own update); 3 trials per scene with different R
              seeds; figures are the fastest trial; every trial faster than
              the original by 0.3 to 1.2%, none slower; player state equal to
              the original at every update. Enhanced, same method: quiet
              -0.30..-0.09%, moving -0.19..-0.12%, moving and firing
              -0.20..-0.04%, death and respawn -0.16..+0.01% (steady); duels
              -1.00..+0.18%; street after a duel +0.03..+0.12%)

  Changes     1.0: the town and duels on the Next's hardware sprite layer at
              the original's pace; the original loading screen; Sinclair's 48K
              ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); the game's speed
              restored after every hook; eight cheats from the archive, ammo
              and money corrected.
              1.1: Enhanced colours, painted by Jon Attree, chosen on the menu
              and off by default: the town, its figures and the twenty duel
              opponents drawn in colour on the Next's Layer 2 at the
              original's pace. The default build is unchanged from 1.0.

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 3 starts; on the keyboard X and C move
              left and right, A up, 1 down and Q fires. The original game's
              look and pace, its town and duels drawn on the Next's hardware
              sprite layer, with Sinclair's whole 48K ROM so it runs on
              NextZXOS 26.11. The original 48K game with its beeper sound;
              fits a 1MB Next. Enhanced paints the town, its figures and the
              duel opponents in their own colours on the Next's Layer 2, at
              the original's pace; off by default. Known issues: in JNext the
              default runs 0.3 to 1.2 percent faster than the original in
              every scene measured; Enhanced is within 1 percent of the
              original in steady play and duels, and the first second or so of
              a scene or duel can run up to 2.3 percent faster. The wanted
              poster keeps the original picture in Enhanced. Missing: not
              reached in testing: natural play to the end, joysticks; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite ammo
   3  Infinite money
   4  Bandit cannot move
   5  Bandit cannot shoot
   6  No horses
   7  No jumping boys
   8  No townsfolk

  The archive's POKEs checked against this exact 48K release, written where
  the game's loader copies its code from; Infinite ammo and Infinite money
  corrected so the original display and arithmetic still work.

