-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played and approved by the owner 2026-11-07 (Enhanced in a
              review build; 1.1 only tunes its pace closer to the original,
              picture unchanged). Run by script through the real loader in
              JNext 1.1.104 on NextZXOS v2.09 and 26.11 card copies: default,
              Enhanced, and Enhanced with all eight cheats

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 11,500 recorded frames (town and duel): at every
              hook original and patched code compared from the same state,
              every register with R and the original's RAM; 5 deliberately
              broken builds rejected. Enhanced: 159 complete updates (town,
              street bandits, all twenty duel opponents, defeat and return to
              town, opponent collapse) run from the same states as the
              original, every register with R, all 48K, memory paging and
              clock equal, and every Layer 2 picture equal pixel for pixel to
              an independent painting of the original renderer; 7 deliberately
              broken renderers rejected

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: default as 1.0 (18 pace trials, 17
              frozen states, 5,650 beeper pulses, a 12,000-frame restart
              soak). Enhanced: 18 pace trials with player state equal to the
              original at every update; 9 native Layer 2 readbacks equal to
              the independent painting on screen; 20,000-frame soaks per mode;
              beeper writes all at the original clock. The real loader
              (.NEXCLASH) on private NextZXOS v2.09 and 26.11 card copies

  Coverage    Recordings, soaks and fixtures by script: menu, town, duels with
              each opponent, deaths, game over and restart; Enhanced also
              played by the owner; not reached: natural completion, joysticks

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
